264	    /// The largest command that survives one ATT packet.
265	    ///
266	    /// Deliberately not `.withResponse`, which answers 512 on every iPhone: that is the
267	    /// maximum *attribute* length, reachable only because CoreBluetooth silently splits
268	    /// a longer value into ATT prepare/execute writes. The robot's `WriteValue` ignores
269	    /// `options["offset"]`, so those fragments arrive as separate commands instead of
270	    /// being reassembled. `.withoutResponse` reports `ATT_MTU - 3`, the only figure that
271	    /// describes what actually fits — even though the command characteristic accepts
272	    /// write-with-response only, and that is the write type used.
